From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:11:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 132/151] Find: match whole word and . matches newline

Two new find options, persisted like the others. Match whole word
rejects matches glued to word chars on either side, also for patterns
that start or end with a non-word char (.foo, foo-), in normal and
regex mode. ". matches newline" shows only in regex mode and sets the
regex dot-all and multi-line flags.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

